"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkaam_docs=globalThis.webpackChunkaam_docs||[]).push([[8130],{7735(t){t.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"aam-v1.1","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/aam-v1.1","editUrl":"https://github.com/ininids/aam/blog/2026-05-15-aam-v1.1.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-05-15-aam-v1.1.md","title":"AAM v1.1 \u2014 Quotes in Lists, Multiline, and More","description":"AAM v1.1 is here with a set of quality-of-life improvements, including quoted items in lists, inline objects, relative path resolution, and a built-in formatter.","date":"2026-05-15T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"AAM","permalink":"/blog/tags/aam","description":"AAM tag description"},{"inline":false,"label":"Feature","permalink":"/blog/tags/feature","description":"Feature tag description"}],"readingTime":1.27,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Nikita Goncharov","title":"AAM author","url":"https://www.ininids.in.rs","page":{"permalink":"/blog/authors/i-ni-ni-ds"},"socials":{"telegram":"https://t.me/ininids","github":"https://github.com/ininids","newsletter":"https://www.ininids.in.rs"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/INiNiDS.png","key":"INiNiDS"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"aam-v1.1","title":"AAM v1.1 \u2014 Quotes in Lists, Multiline, and More","authors":["INiNiDS"],"tags":["aam","feature"]},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"LLMs and Robots","permalink":"/blog/llms-and-robots"}},"content":"AAM v1.1 is here with a set of quality-of-life improvements, including quoted items in lists, inline objects, relative path resolution, and a built-in formatter.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New in v1.1\\n\\n### Quoted Items in Lists\\n\\nList items can now be wrapped in double (`\\"`) or single (`\'`) quotes. Commas inside quoted items are handled correctly \u2014 no more false separators:\\n\\n```aam\\nitems = [\\"rust, aam\\", \'single, quoted\', plain_value]\\n```\\n\\nThis creates three items: `rust, aam`, `single, quoted`, and `plain_value`. Quotes are automatically stripped from the final values.\\n\\n### Inline Objects\\n\\nValues can now be inline objects, making nested configurations more natural:\\n\\n```aam\\nserver = { host = \\"localhost\\", port = 8080, debug = true }\\nconfig = { database = { host = \\"db.local\\", port = 5432 } }\\n```\\n\\nFields are comma-separated, and nesting `{}` is fully supported.\\n\\n### Multiline Directives\\n\\nMultiline support for `@schema`, `@type`, and other directive blocks has been improved. Blocks spanning multiple lines are accumulated and processed correctly, with proper brace-balance tracking:\\n\\n```aam\\n@schema Player {\\n    name: string\\n    score: i32\\n    tags: list<string>\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Relative Path Resolution\\n\\n`@import` and `@derive` paths are now resolved relative to the file they\'re written in:\\n\\n```aam\\n@import ./schemas/base.aam\\n@derive ./types/player.aam::Player\\n```\\n\\n### Built-in Formatter\\n\\nAAM now includes a formatter that automatically formats your files. It supports smart schema formatting, directive hoisting, configurable indentation, and key sorting.\\n\\n### AOT Compilation\\n\\nThe new AOT (Ahead-of-Time) compilation path detects simple files and uses a fast single-pass parse, falling back to the full pipeline only when needed for multiline blocks or directives.\\n\\n---\\n\\nCheck the [updated documentation](/docs/using/types) for full details on all features."},{"id":"llms-and-robots","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/llms-and-robots","editUrl":"https://github.com/ininids/aam/blog/2026-03-4-update.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-03-4-update.md","title":"LLMs and Robots","description":"New update is coming up with a llms.txt and robots.txt new files for search engines and AI.","date":"2026-03-04T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"AAM","permalink":"/blog/tags/aam","description":"AAM tag description"},{"inline":false,"label":"Update","permalink":"/blog/tags/update","description":"Update tag description"}],"readingTime":0.12,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Nikita Goncharov","title":"AAM author","url":"https://www.ininids.in.rs","page":{"permalink":"/blog/authors/i-ni-ni-ds"},"socials":{"telegram":"https://t.me/ininids","github":"https://github.com/ininids","newsletter":"https://www.ininids.in.rs"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/INiNiDS.png","key":"INiNiDS"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"llms-and-robots","title":"LLMs and Robots","authors":["INiNiDS"],"tags":["aam","update"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"AAM v1.1 \u2014 Quotes in Lists, Multiline, and More","permalink":"/blog/aam-v1.1"},"nextItem":{"title":"Starting AAM","permalink":"/blog/starting-aam"}},"content":"New update is coming up with a llms.txt and robots.txt new files for search engines and AI.\\nAnd added [examples](@site/docs/examples.md)"},{"id":"starting-aam","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/starting-aam","editUrl":"https://github.com/ininids/aam/blog/2026-03-2-first-blog-post.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-03-2-first-blog-post.md","title":"Starting AAM","description":"Let\'s start with AAM!","date":"2026-03-02T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"AAM","permalink":"/blog/tags/aam","description":"AAM tag description"}],"readingTime":0.32,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Nikita Goncharov","title":"AAM author","url":"https://www.ininids.in.rs","page":{"permalink":"/blog/authors/i-ni-ni-ds"},"socials":{"telegram":"https://t.me/ininids","github":"https://github.com/ininids","newsletter":"https://www.ininids.in.rs"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/INiNiDS.png","key":"INiNiDS"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"starting-aam","title":"Starting AAM","authors":["INiNiDS"],"tags":["aam"]},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"LLMs and Robots","permalink":"/blog/llms-and-robots"}},"content":"Let\'s start with AAM!\\n\\n## AAM?\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\nModern,  \\nEasy,  \\nBest  \\nAAM is a really good aliasing format  \\nNeeds easy configuration? OK  \\nNeeds fast parsing? OK  \\nNeeds type safety? OK  \\nNeeds transform hard to easy? OKKKKKKK\\n\\n## Example\\n\\n```aam\\nhost = localhost\\nport = 8080\\n```\\n\\nit\'s all. If you say `localhost` you will get `host` from config.\\n\\"What is localhost? It\'s a \\\\{AAM::get(\\"localhost\\")\\\\}\\"\\nReally easy, yes?"}]}}')}}]);